Heroes are a feature rarity that allow specific [[Cards]] placed in the {{Rarity|Champion}} slots to gain an ability. Heroes and the first {{Rarity|Champion}} slot are both unlocked at [[Arenas#Trophy Road|Arena]] 5. Every card with a Hero variation requires 200 {{Icon|I=Hero Shard}} to be unlocked. All Heroes have an ability that the original card doesn't have, similar to {{Rarity|Champion}} cards.

==Summary==
*The {{Rarity|Champion}} slot is unlocked at Arena 5, while the Wild slot is unlocked at Arena 10.
*Heroes have a unique gimmick which is shared with {{Rarity|Champion}} cards. Just like {{Rarity|Champion}} cards, Abilities are accessible just above the player's “hand” in [[Basics of Battle|battle]]. They cost [[Elixir]] to cast, granting the last played Heroic cards their special ability depending on the Hero, and will only stay as long as the selected Hero that you want to use the ability of is alive.
**The average Elixir cost in the [[Battle Decks|deck]] menu only counts the base Elixir cost instead of both the base and the ability.
*Only two Heroes can be in a deck at a time, and only in the Hero and Wild slots. Those slots are also shared with {{Rarity|Champion}} card, which means that the player can have 1 Hero and 1 {{Rarity|Champion}} at the same time.
*[[Clone]] can be used on a Heroic card, but the Heroic card's ability will only be used by the original.
*When a Hero activates their ability, but did not start casting it before they are defeated, the Elixir spent on the ability will be refunded once they are defeated.
*Heroes can be upgraded by the base card's Wild Cards of respective rarity.

